Replaces: howdy
Description: C++ facial-recognition authentication for Linux
 Howdy Next is a C++ rewrite of Howdy. It provides a PAM module and
 CLI for Windows Hello-style facial authentication on Linux.
 .
 This unofficial package vendors OpenCV 5 (not yet in Debian main) and
 yyjson 0.12. Face models are not included; run
 "sudo howdy download-models" after install.
 .
 Howdy is weaker than a password. Never use it as the sole
 authentication method. This package does not enable PAM automatically.
